  ('400723847991751666', 'Nightfall', 1988, 'Science Fiction', 'Paul Mayersberg, Dariusz Wolski', 'Paul Mayersberg', 'David Birney, Sarah Douglas, Alexis Kanner, Andra Millian, Starr Andreeff, Charley Hayward, Jonathan Emerson, Susie Lindeman', 'PG-13', 'The people of the planet Aeon, blessed with three suns, have never experienced night. When an archeological excavation uncovers evidence of an ancient catastrophe, all signs point towards the impending darkness of the very Nightfall. Panic erupts as the suns slowly disappear one by one. Science struggles against superstition as the people race to comprehend the approaching Nightfall... the end of the world as they know it. Based on Isaac Asimov''s classic story "Nightfall" voted "The Greatest Science-Fiction Story of All Time."', 'The people of the planet Aeon, blessed with three suns, have never experienced night. When an archeological excavation uncovers evidence of an ancient catastrophe, all signs point towards the impending darkness of the very Nightfall. Panic erupts as the suns slowly disappear one by one. Science struggles against superstition as the people race to comprehend the approaching Nightfall... the end of the world as they know it. Based on Isaac Asimov''s classic story "Nightfall" voted "The Greatest Science-Fiction Story of All Time."', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/9BLBKuNRSjt2Ono9vkao69LtRKz.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:72339'),
  ('395777172373800346', 'Nightfall', 1999, 'Drama', 'Fred Kelemen, Fred Kelemen, Suzanne Schmitt', 'Fred Kelemen', 'Adolfo Assor, Thomas Baumann, Isa Hochgerner, Verena Jasch, Wolfgang Michael, Urs Remond, Daniela Roque-Magalhaes', null, 'A largely plotless, fado-scored journey through the gloomy cobblestone streets, zombie bars, and fetid basements of a sordid harbor town populated by German-speaking sots and Portuguese guest workers. An unhappy young couple, Leni and Anton, quarrel and split separately into the rat’s ass of the evening. Everyone is looking for love, but no one finds any—although Leni does pick up a trick.', 'A largely plotless, fado-scored journey through the gloomy cobblestone streets, zombie bars, and fetid basements of a sordid harbor town populated by German-speaking sots and Portuguese guest workers. An unhappy young couple, Leni and Anton, quarrel and split separately into the rat’s ass of the evening. Everyone is looking for love, but no one finds any—although Leni does pick up a trick.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/sHVOj2PnAXVYsHmuw8HgO4FkjVE.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:218150'),
